### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 05 - HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP (HITL) GOVERNANCE & APPROVAL FLOW
###
### When an agent invokes a tool with operation = NETWORK_OUTBOUND
### and the session autonomy level is SUPERVISED (default), the
### ToolInvocationGuard throws RequiresApprovalException instead of
### executing the tool. The AgentLoop saves an AWAITING_APPROVAL
### checkpoint and returns a 202 response describing what needs approval.
###
### Two paths to approve/deny:
###   A) REST endpoints (tested here):
###        POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
###        POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/deny?agentRole=coordinator
###   B) Goal string in run/run-async (legacy in-band method):
###        goal: "/approve"  or  goal: "/deny"
###
### Checkpoint state machine:
###   AWAITING_APPROVAL → agent paused, saved to SQLite
###   COMPLETED         → after successful approve + resume
###   FAILED            → after deny or approval timeout
###
### Autonomy level note (Phase 64-A fix A2):
###   Sessions created with FULL autonomy no longer need approval for
###   NETWORK_OUTBOUND tools. See 14_budget_governance.http FLOW D.
###
### Prerequisites: Amsha Agent serve mode, AMSHA_LLM_API_KEY + GITHUB_TOKEN set.
###   GithubTool is the only built-in tool with ToolOperation=NETWORK_OUTBOUND.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW A: REST APPROVE
# Create session → trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL → poll status → approve
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-1] Create session for approve flow
# @name approveSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-2] Run async - ask coordinator to use GitHub tool
# GithubTool has ToolOperation=NETWORK_OUTBOUND + session autonomy=SUPERVISED (default).
# ToolInvocationGuard throws RequiresApprovalException.
# AgentLoop saves AWAITING_APPROVAL checkpoint and returns 202.
# Expect: 202 {"toolName":"github","paramsJson":"{...}","sessionId":"..."}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-3] Poll status - should show AWAITING_APPROVAL
# Run immediately after HITL-2, before approving.
# Expect: {"sessionId":"...","status":"AWAITING_APPROVAL","steps":[...],"failReason":null}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-4] APPROVE via dedicated REST endpoint
# agentRole query param must match the role in the saved checkpoint.
# The agent resumes from the checkpoint with AutonomyLevel.FULL for this one invocation.
# Audit event APPROVAL_GRANTED is mandatory - agent halts if write fails.
# Expect: 200 {"answer":"...","totalInputTokens":N,"totalOutputTokens":N}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-5] Poll status after approve - should now be COMPLETED
# Expect: {"sessionId":"...","status":"COMPLETED","steps":[...],"failReason":null}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW B: REST DENY
# Create session → trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL → deny → check FAILED
# NOTE: HITL-8 (deny) must run BEFORE HITL-9 (status after deny).
#       Previous version of this file had them reversed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-6] Create session for deny flow
# @name denySession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-7] Run async - trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL
# Expect: 202 (agent paused pending approval)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-7a] Optional: Poll status to confirm AWAITING_APPROVAL before denying
# Expect: status = AWAITING_APPROVAL
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-8] DENY via dedicated REST endpoint
# This MUST run before HITL-9 (status poll after deny).
# AgentSessionService.deny() calls agentStore.markFailed() and removes the heartbeat.
# Audit event APPROVAL_DENIED is mandatory.
# Expect: 200 {"status":"DENIED","session":"..."}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/deny?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-9] Status after deny - should be FAILED
# Expect: {"sessionId":"...","status":"FAILED","failReason":"Human denied via REST"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW B2: DENY VIA GOAL STRING (in-band method on a separate session)
# Using goal="/deny" in run-async on an AWAITING_APPROVAL session.
# Note: use this on a DIFFERENT session from HITL-6/7/8/9 above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-8a] Create fresh session for in-band deny test
# @name denyGoalSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-8b] Trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denyGoalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-8c] Deny via goal="/deny" in run-async
# AgentSessionService.runAsync() special-cases "/deny" → marks checkpoint FAILED.
# Functionally identical to the REST /deny endpoint.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denyGoalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/deny",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denyGoalSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denyGoalSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW C: APPROVE VIA GOAL STRING (legacy in-band method)
# Sending goal="/approve" in run-async triggers the same approval path.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-10] Create session
# @name goalApproveSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-11] Trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "View the rsrini7/amsha repository using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-11a] Poll status - confirm AWAITING_APPROVAL before approving
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-12] Approve via goal="/approve" in run-async
# AgentSessionService.runAsync() special-cases "/approve" → sets AutonomyLevel.FULL
# for the resume. Expect: agent resumes and completes.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}



###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW D: APPROVAL TIMEOUT (manual observation)
# amsha.governance.approval-timeout-seconds (default: 300)
# After the timeout, ApprovalTimeoutNotifier fires and marks FAILED.
# After Phase 64-C2: ChannelApprovalTimeoutDispatcher routes to correct channel.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-13] Create session and trigger approval - then wait for timeout
# @name timeoutSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{timeoutSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### Wait 5+ minutes (or reduce approval-timeout-seconds in application.yaml for testing).
### Then poll status - must be FAILED.
### Log to watch: "ApprovalTimeout fired for session ... - marking FAILED"
### Audit event: CHECKPOINT_FAILED with reason "Approval timeout"

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{timeoutSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{timeoutSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR / EDGE CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-14] Approve on non-existent session → expect 409 CONFLICT
# AgentSessionService.approve() returns 409 if no AWAITING_APPROVAL checkpoint found.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-15] Approve on already-COMPLETED session → expect 409 CONFLICT
# No pending approval checkpoint - approve has nothing to resume.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-16] Approve without API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [HITL-17] Deny without API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/deny
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [HITL-18] Deny on non-existent session → expect 409 CONFLICT or 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000/deny?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-19] Rate limit probe - this endpoint always returns 200 with valid key
# Useful for confirming the rate limiter does not block valid repeated requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
